{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3374","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3374","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3374\",\"parent_revision\":\"1d98475005cdf83463da827ca149de78692cbe14771e8d41ce04371e383e7f4b\",\"root_revision\":\"1d98475005cdf83463da827ca149de78692cbe14771e8d41ce04371e383e7f4b\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-01\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThis repo's own testing standard (`python-engineering:python3-core` skill, `references/tool-library-registry.md`) states plainly: \\\"pytest-mock exclusively (never unittest.mock)\\\" and \\\"NEVER use unittest.mock directly... REQUIRED: mocker.Mock() not Mock()\\\". `plugins/development-harness`'s test suite has drifted substantially from this.\\n\\nMeasured directly against the current test tree (`tests/`, `tests_backlog/`, `tests_sam/`):\\n- 48 test files import `unittest.mock` directly (`from unittest.mock import ...` / `import unittest.mock` / `from unittest import mock`).\\n- 404 call sites use `MagicMock(...)`, `Mock(...)`, or `unittest.mock.patch`/`mock.patch(...)` directly, versus only 32 files using the mandated `mocker: MockerFixture` fixture (`mocker.patch`/`mocker.Mock`).\\n\\nThis was surfaced while verifying new test code added in PR #3366 (`tests/test_dispatch_capability_gate.py`, `tests_backlog/test_beads_backend.py`) against the standard \u2014 that new code is compliant (uses `mocker` exclusively, no `unittest.mock` import), but it sits inside a suite where the surrounding convention has already drifted, including in files touched incidentally by that PR (`tests_backlog/test_beads_backend.py`'s pre-existing `_make_runner()` helper uses `MagicMock(spec=BdRunner)` directly).\\n\\nImpact: the documented standard is not enforced by any lint rule (ruff has no rule that flags `unittest.mock` imports), so drift is invisible until someone reads the guide and checks by hand, as happened here. New tests added without deliberately checking the guide will keep copying the surrounding (non-compliant) pattern rather than the documented one.\\n\\nUser-provided context: no fix approach has been decided \u2014 whether to do a repo-wide mechanical migration, add a ruff/custom lint rule to catch new `unittest.mock` imports going forward (so the standard is enforced rather than just documented), or something else, is a decision for grooming, not this filing.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: User request during PR #3366 review, prompted by a check of new test code against the python-engineering:python3-core guide\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-01\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"2c0c4e00efc730c4e0d5411df710775069aeb368a259f8ab6a2898dca3e8bb84\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABR0q1PA\"}"}